## Nitrogen
component-nitrogen = Nitrogen
component-nitrogen-description-novice = The gas that makes up most of the air — about three quarters. It neither burns nor supports burning. Liquid nitrogen boils at −196 °C and instantly freezes flowers and fruit.
component-nitrogen-description-school = Nitrogen is chemically inactive, which is why crisp packets are filled with it: the food does not oxidise.
component-nitrogen-safety-school = Liquid nitrogen causes cold burns, and its vapour displaces oxygen in a closed room.
